WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.374
The course can be summarized as a practical operating routine.

2
00:00:04.374 --> 00:00:07.436
First, define the claim and the decision.

3
00:00:07.436 --> 00:00:17.060
What is being asserted, who needs to act, and what could go wrong if the organization acts too quickly or too slowly?

4
00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:21.434
This step prevents the review from becoming an open-ended debate.

5
00:00:21.434 --> 00:00:27.121
It ties evidence collection to the decision the organization actually has to make.

6
00:00:27.121 --> 00:00:30.183
Second, preserve context and evaluate the source.

7
00:00:30.183 --> 00:00:37.182
Capture the artifact, surrounding records, time window, collection method, and chain of custody details that matter.

8
00:00:37.182 --> 00:00:45.056
Ask whether the source is reliable over time and whether the specific information is credible in this case.

9
00:00:45.056 --> 00:00:52.055
Provenance is often the difference between a useful artifact and a persuasive object with uncertain meaning.

10
00:00:52.055 --> 00:00:54.679
Third, verify evidence and test alternatives.

11
00:00:54.679 --> 00:00:57.304
Look for independent corroboration where possible.

12
00:00:57.304 --> 00:01:03.865
Check whether timestamps, identity context, system records, approval paths, and telemetry support the same conclusion.

13
00:01:03.865 --> 00:01:08.677
Write down assumptions and ask what else could explain the evidence.

14
00:01:08.677 --> 00:01:16.551
Inconsistency deserves attention, but the answer may be benign error, incomplete collection, or process drift rather than deception.

15
00:01:16.551 --> 00:01:20.488
Finally, communicate in decision-ready language and improve the system.

16
00:01:20.488 --> 00:01:22.675
Separate facts, assumptions, and judgments.

17
00:01:22.675 --> 00:01:25.737
Use confidence language that fits the evidence.

18
00:01:25.737 --> 00:01:34.486
Escalate through the right ownership path, document what was preserved and why, and avoid spreading sensitive or misleading material unnecessarily.

19
00:01:34.486 --> 00:01:39.735
After the review, update playbooks, trusted channel lists, approval workflows, and training.

20
00:01:39.735 --> 00:01:43.672
Counter-deception becomes valuable when it is repeatable under pressure.
